# Pinned Aether toolchain version — the single place to bump.
#
# Pinned so a fresh clone (bootstrap.sh) and CI install the exact tested
# toolchain instead of whatever "latest" happens to be that day. bootstrap.sh
# sources this file; override at the shell to test a bump
# (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.850.0 ./bootstrap.sh`).

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA.
#
# 0.841.0 (2026-10-23), from the 0.818–0.824 range the tracking commits verified.
# What the jump to 0.841 broke here, fixed in the same commit:
#   - std.json no longer exports `stringify` / `json_create_string`; the exported
#     spellings are `encode` / `str` (same signatures).
#   - E0200/E0202: a `ptr` from `list.get` / `map.get` can no longer be
#     interpolated or assigned to a string; the typed getters `list.get_string` /
#     `map.get_string` are required.
#   - E0902: a `spec.before_each` callback that captures the WebDriver handle
#     needs the handle parameter marked `@keep ptr` (0.818+ ownership checks).
#   - selaenium 0.7.0 does not build on 0.841; the dependency is now 0.14.2,
#     which is built on 0.841 itself.
# Verified on 0.841.0: conformance (20), unit (45), streaming and
# TLS suites pass; every cmd/ binary builds; the component suites compile and run
# against selaenium 0.14.2 (see README "Requirements" for the run record).
#
# 0.931.0 (2026-11-20), floor move with the code change that 0.927.0 forced:
#   - E0202: a `ptr` from `list.get` / `map.get` given to a `string` parameter
#     is refused outright (0.927.0). The string-list readers in
#     datastar/module.ae, harness/stories, harness/storaebook and the
#     conformance test now use `list.get_string` / `map.get_string`.
# Verified on the released 0.931.0, Linux x86_64 (cachyos): conformance (20),
# unit (45), streaming and TLS pass; every cmd/ binary builds; and the six
# component suites (47 tests) pass under xvfb with the harness running.
# Caveat: those component suites ran against selaenium's main branch (via
# `ae run --override`), because the released selaenium 0.14.2 does not compile
# on 0.931.0 (its drivermgr hits the same E0202). tests/component/aether.toml
# still names 0.14.2 until selaenium cuts a release that builds on 0.931.
# 0.935.0 (2026-11-22): a TRACKING bump from 0.931.0, no new primitive needed and no
# source change (the hard floor below stays 0.931.0). Verified on the released 0.935.0, Linux
# x86_64 (cachyos): conformance (20), unit (45), streaming and TLS pass; every cmd/ binary builds.
# The Selenium component suites were not re-run.
AETHER_REF=v0.935.0

# Hard floor: the OLDEST ae this repo is known to build/pass on (0.931.0 only
# because that is the one release verified after the 0.927.0 E0202 change). bootstrap.sh
# rejects an already-on-PATH ae below this (installs the pin instead). Never
# below the pin while the pin is the only verified version.
AETHER_MIN=0.931.0

